      "writtenOn": "2025-06-20T23:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, for `Result\u003cT*, E\u003e`, `nullptr` wouldn\u0027t be ambiguous and default to using `T*` as the type since no additional constructor conversions are necessary so resolution ordering would prefer that over converting the `nullptr` to a `unique_ptr\u003cE\u003e` which would take one additional constructor conversion. I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s possible to disable the default overload of `unique_ptr\u003cT\u003e` with `nullptr` without doing something like extending it as a private type and hiding that constructor or something.",
      "parentUuid": "6ab1ea7c_83135354",
      "revId": "ab11c5c57b8de8a637fb1c6ff98082daee21a426",
